  {
    "id": "script_1754465356284_ksjkkzk8r",
    "title": "Watermelon Mystery",
    "rounds": 3,
    "background": "In the height of summer, the cicadas chirp noisily. Wang Apo's watermelon field ushers in the most fruitful day of the year. The red, sandy, and sweet watermelons are the favorite of the village children. However, on the morning of the harvest, Wang Apo discovers that her carefully cultivated 'Melon King' is missing! The melon vine has been cut by a sharp weapon, leaving only an empty stem. The villagers are talking about it. Some say it was stolen by a wild animal, some say it was a prank by a naughty child, and some say it was a jealous competitor. What is the truth? Only by finding the Melon King can the mystery of the missing watermelon be solved.",
    "characters": [
      {
        "id": "wangPo",
        "name": "Wang Cuihua",
        "identity": "Melon farmer, the only watermelon grower in the village",
        "personality": "Hardworking and simple, straightforward, loves melons as much as her own life",
        "isMainCharacter": true
      },
      {
        "id": "liXiao",
        "name": "Li Xiaoming",
        "identity": "A naughty child in the village, famous for being mischievous",
        "personality": "Naughty, curious, adventurous",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      },
      {
        "id": "zhangSan",
        "name": "Zhang San",
        "identity": "The owner of the village grocery store, always smiling",
        "personality": "Shrewd, slick, well-informed",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      }
    ],
    "roundContents": [
      {
        "round": 1,
        "plot": "Wang Apo is anxious when she finds the Melon King is missing. She first finds Li Xiaoming, who often plays near her melon field, to ask if he has seen any suspicious people. Li Xiaoming stammers and says that yesterday evening he saw Zhang San wandering suspiciously near the melon field with a sack. Zhang San flatly denies it, saying that he was just fishing by the small river next to the melon field.",
        "privateClues": {
          "wangPo": "The cut on the melon vine is very neat, as if made by a knife, not bitten by an animal. There are some scattered cigarette butts around the Melon King, which are not the brand of cigarettes I smoke.",
          "liXiao": "I did see Uncle Zhang San going towards the melon field with a sack yesterday, but he rarely goes there to fish, and I didn't see his fishing gear by the river.",
          "zhangSan": "I did go fishing by the river yesterday, but I didn't catch anything, so I was in a bad mood and smoked a few cigarettes. The sack is for fishing gear, I'm innocent!"
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 2,
        "plot": "Wang Apo confronts Zhang San, and the two argue endlessly. Li Xiaoming adds fuel to the fire, saying that he saw Zhang San carry the sack home. Wang Apo demands to search Zhang San's grocery store, but Zhang San firmly refuses. During the argument, Wang Apo notices a fresh scratch on Zhang San's hand. Zhang San explains that he was accidentally scratched by a fishhook.",
        "privateClues": {
          "wangPo": "The scratch on Zhang San's hand is long and deep, it doesn't look like it could be caused by a fishhook. His shop has recently stocked some new goods, all of which are high-end watermelon knives that are only available in the city.",
          "liXiao": "Uncle Zhang San is usually not willing to smoke such expensive cigarettes. I think I've seen the cigarette butts near the melon field yesterday, they are the brand he usually smokes. Also, his shoes had fresh mud on them yesterday, which is very similar to the soil in the melon field.",
          "zhangSan": "Damn Li Xiaoming, he must be jealous of my recent good business! The scratch on my hand was really caused by a fishhook. I sell watermelon knives to make it convenient for customers to cut watermelons, not to steal them!"
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 3,
        "plot": "Wang Apo insists on searching Zhang San's shop. In the end, with the mediation of the village chief, Zhang San reluctantly agrees. During the search, the Melon King is not found. However, in the corner of Zhang San's backyard, Wang Apo finds a discarded sack covered in mud, with some watermelon rinds inside!",
        "privateClues": {
          "wangPo": "The watermelon rinds in the sack are obviously not from ordinary watermelons. The flesh is dark in color and very sweet, exactly the same as my Melon King! Also, the sack has the unique fertilizer smell of my melon field.",
          "liXiao": "I saw Uncle Zhang San drag the sack to the backyard yesterday, and he secretly burned something. The smoke was very thick and the smell was strange, a bit like burning watermelon rinds.",
          "zhangSan": "That... that was thrown in my backyard by someone else! I have no idea what's inside! Someone must be framing me! I recently bought a batch of inferior watermelons and threw them in the backyard because I was afraid of affecting my reputation!"
        }
      }
    ],
    "createdAt": 1754465356284,
    "createdBy": "system"
  },
  {
    "id": "script_1754466654535_cctfu8f3l",
    "title": "The Secret of the Grape Vineyard",
    "rounds": 3,
    "background": "In sunny Tuscany, the air is filled with the sweet scent of grapes. The Vittorio Grape Vineyard is one of the most prestigious orchards in this land, famous for its Royal Grapes. However, this year's harvest season is shrouded in a shadow. The old owner, Vittorio Bellini, suddenly passed away, and the cause of death is a mystery. It was officially announced as a heart attack, but there are various speculations circulating, the most prevalent of which is that Vittorio hid a priceless secret recipe. This recipe is related to the secret of the unique flavor of the Royal Grapes and has attracted countless people's covetousness. Now, Vittorio's funeral has just ended, and his will has not yet been announced. Everyone has their own ulterior motives, waiting for the final truth to be revealed. And you, Vittorio's only daughter, Emilia Bellini, will have to face all this.",
    "characters": [
      {
        "id": "emilia",
        "name": "Emilia Bellini",
        "identity": "Vittorio Bellini's daughter, the heir to the grape vineyard",
        "personality": "Smart, independent, slightly melancholic, saddened by her father's death, but also suspects that there is more to it.",
        "isMainCharacter": true
      },
      {
        "id": "marco",
        "name": "Marco Ricci",
        "identity": "The old butler of the grape vineyard, has worked for the Bellini family for over thirty years",
        "personality": "Loyal and honest, taciturn, but seems to be hiding some secrets.",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      },
      {
        "id": "sofia",
        "name": "Sofia Graziani",
        "identity": "The owner of the local town's flower shop, has a close relationship with the Bellini family",
        "personality": "Enthusiastic and cheerful, gossipy, well-informed, knows everything about the grape vineyard.",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      }
    ],
    "roundContents": [
      {
        "round": 1,
        "plot": "After the funeral, Emilia returns to her father's study, hoping to find some clues. The study is filled with books and documents, and the air is filled with the smell of old paper. Marco is packing things, looking a little absent-minded. Sofia comes to offer her condolences with a bouquet of white lilies and comforts Emilia. She mentions that old Vittorio seemed to be looking for something before he died, and often locked himself in the study.",
        "privateClues": {
          "emilia": "You find a crumpled note in your father's desk drawer, which says 'Royal Grapes, under the moonlight, the third row.'",
          "marco": "You see Emilia enter the study and feel uneasy. You know that old Vittorio was hiding some secrets, and these secrets may affect your future. You hide a diary about the secrets of the grape vineyard.",
          "sofia": "You hear some rumors in the flower shop about the cause of Vittorio's death. Some say he discovered an ancient treasure buried in the grape vineyard. You tell this to Emilia, hoping she can find the truth."
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 2,
        "plot": "Following the hint on the note, Emilia comes to the grape vineyard at night. Under the moonlight, she counts to the third row of vines and finds an iron box buried at the root of one of them. Inside the iron box is a letter and an old photo. The letter is from Vittorio to Emilia, confessing that he is not her biological father, and that her biological father is someone else. The photo is of a young man. Marco also discovers Emilia's actions and tries to stop her from investigating further, but is questioned by Emilia. Sofia reveals that Emilia's biological father was once a gardener in the grape vineyard, but disappeared mysteriously many years ago.",
        "privateClues": {
          "emilia": "The letter mentions that your biological father's name is Riccardo Graziani, Sofia's brother. He disappeared after a dispute with Vittorio over the use of a certain pesticide.",
          "marco": "You know what's in the iron box, it's old Vittorio's biggest secret. You once promised him to keep the secret, but now you are starting to waver. You are afraid that Emilia will discover the deal between you and old Vittorio, that you secretly helped him replace the grape recipe.",
          "sofia": "You are surprised that Emilia is Riccardo's daughter. You always thought Riccardo was dead. Back then, you witnessed the argument between Riccardo and Vittorio, and then Riccardo disappeared. You suspect that Vittorio killed your brother."
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 3,
        "plot": "Emilia finds Sofia and questions her about Riccardo. Sofia confesses the truth of that year and accuses Vittorio of being the murderer. Emilia decides to investigate Riccardo's disappearance. She finds Marco and hopes he can help. Marco finally has a change of heart and tells Emilia that Vittorio did have a dispute with Riccardo back then, but he did not intentionally kill him. Riccardo accidentally fell into a deep well in the grape vineyard. Vittorio, afraid of taking responsibility, chose to hide the truth and sealed the well. Emilia, led by Marco, finds the deep well, and the truth is finally revealed.",
        "privateClues": {
          "emilia": "You find a pocket watch engraved with 'RG' in the deep well, which is your biological father's relic. You realize that although your father Vittorio hid the truth, he may have also carried a heavy burden of guilt.",
          "marco": "You are finally free from the condemnation of your conscience and tell Emilia the truth. You hope that Emilia can forgive old Vittorio and continue to protect the glory of the grape vineyard. You find old Vittorio's notes on the pesticide recipe under the grape vineyard, which says 'Royal Grapes need to be cared for with love.'",
          "sofia": "After learning the cause of your brother's death, you are deeply saddened. But you also understand that the truth being revealed is the best comfort for your brother. You hope that Emilia can re-operate the grape vineyard and let Riccardo's spirit live on forever. You tell Emilia that the real secret of the Royal Grapes is love, not pesticides."
        }
      }
    ],
    "createdAt": 1754466654535,
    "createdBy": "system"
  },
  {
    "id": "script_1754467058265_9chltjj5k",
    "title": "The Secret Under the Spotlight",
    "rounds": 3,
    "background": "The star-studded stage, the brilliant lights, this is the arena that the nation's top dancers dream of - the 'Dance Miracle' national dance selection competition. Every year, countless dancers with dreams gather here, just to compete for the championship trophy that symbolizes honor and the opportunity to sign with a top brokerage company. This year's competition is particularly fierce, the competitors are unprecedentedly strong, and various rumors are rampant. On the eve of the semi-finals, a very promising dark horse contestant suddenly announced her withdrawal, with a vague reason, as if hiding an ulterior secret. Around this withdrawal incident, everyone has their own ulterior motives. The dream of dancing, the desire for fame, the shadow of jealousy, are intertwined into a complex picture. Everyone wants to show their most perfect self under the spotlight, but the spotlight also illuminates the shadows hidden in the dark. This competition is by no means just a contest of dance skills, but also a contest of human nature and desire. You, as a highly anticipated seed contestant, can you clear the fog, realize your dance dream, and uncover the truth hidden behind the withdrawal?",
    "characters": [
      {
        "id": "character1",
        "name": "Amy Chen",
        "identity": "Ballet dancer, known as the 'Black Swan'",
        "personality": "Cold and arrogant on the outside, but longs for recognition on the inside, has extremely high demands on herself, slightly neurotic",
        "isMainCharacter": true
      },
      {
        "id": "character2",
        "name": "Li Wei",
        "identity": "Staff of the event organizing committee",
        "personality": "Slick and worldly, good at everything, good at observation, well-informed",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      }
    ],
    "roundContents": [
      {
        "round": 1,
        "plot": "The day before the semi-finals of the selection competition, Amy is practicing alone in the dance studio. The high-intensity training has exhausted her physically and mentally. Li Wei comes to inform Amy that the highly acclaimed contestant Zhao Linlin has suddenly announced her withdrawal, citing physical discomfort. Li Wei implies to Amy that Zhao Linlin's withdrawal is an opportunity for her, and she should seize it. Although Amy is calm on the surface, her heart is full of doubts and unease. She vaguely feels that Zhao Linlin's withdrawal is not simple, and seems to be hiding some secret. Outside the dance studio, the lights are dim, and a figure flashes, as if monitoring her every move.",
        "privateClues": {
          "character1": "You receive an anonymous letter with only one sentence: 'Watch your step.' The envelope has a faint jasmine perfume smell.",
          "character2": "Before Zhao Linlin withdrew, she had repeatedly asked the organizing committee for information about Amy's background. She seemed very interested in Amy's past."
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 2,
        "plot": "Amy finds Li Wei and asks for more details about Zhao Linlin's withdrawal. Li Wei stammers and only says that Zhao Linlin was under too much pressure and her physical condition did not allow her to continue the competition. Amy does not believe his words. She finds that Li Wei's attitude is a bit evasive, as if he is hiding something. Amy remembers the warning in the anonymous letter and begins to pay attention to the people and things around her. She finds that the other contestants are also looking at her strangely, as if she has become the target of public criticism. During rehearsal, Amy accidentally sprains her foot. Although the injury is not serious, it makes her more vigilant. She begins to suspect that someone is secretly framing her.",
        "privateClues": {
          "character1": "Your ballet shoes have been tampered with. The soles seem to have been smeared with some oily substance, which caused you to almost slip. If you smell it carefully, it smells a bit like the hand cream your mother uses.",
          "character2": "You find in the surveillance footage that the night before she withdrew, Zhao Linlin had secretly entered Amy's dance studio. But the footage is very blurry and it is impossible to see what she did."
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 3,
        "plot": "On the day of the final, Amy meets Li Wei backstage. Li Wei tells her that the organizing committee has investigated and found that Zhao Linlin withdrew because she discovered that Amy had used banned drugs in a competition abroad. He warns Amy that if she withdraws voluntarily now, the organizing committee can announce to the public that it is due to physical discomfort, thus preserving her reputation. Amy is shocked. She has never touched banned drugs. She knows that someone is deliberately framing her. She realizes that this is not just about the competition, but a slander against her life. She decides not to be silent anymore, to find the mastermind and clear her name.",
        "privateClues": {
          "character1": "You recall that during the competition abroad, you received a 'mysterious gift,' a bottle of nutrient solution that you never ordered. You didn't pay attention to it at the time and threw it away. Now that you think about it, that bottle of nutrient solution was likely the source of the tampered banned drugs.",
          "character2": "You find a photo in Zhao Linlin's room. The photo is of Amy's mother and a strange man. The man is holding a document, which seems to be Amy's drug test report from the competition abroad."
        }
      }
    ],
    "createdAt": 1754467058265,
    "createdBy": "system"
  },
  {
    "id": "script_1754467207980_14dggnb49",
    "title": "The Secret Under the Spotlight",
    "rounds": 3,
    "background": "In the height of summer, the star-studded 'Dance Miracle' national finals are about to kick off. Every year, countless dancers with dreams long to stand on this stage, conquer the audience with their dance, and win glory. However, behind the glamorous facade, there are unknown competitions and secrets. This year's final is particularly eye-catching, because the defending champion, Emilia, not only has to face the challenge of a new dark horse, but also has to deal with a sudden rumor - someone claims that her famous dance steps are not original, but stolen from the posthumous work of the genius dancer, Victor. Public opinion pressure is like a mountain, and Emilia must prove herself in the final, not only with her perfect dance, but also by uncovering the truth and defending her reputation. At the same time, someone hidden in the audience seems to be waiting for an opportunity to reveal a dusty past. Tonight, the spotlight not only illuminates the stage, but also the secrets buried in the dark.",
    "characters": [
      {
        "id": "character1",
        "name": "Emilia Romanova",
        "identity": "Defending champion, 'Dance Miracle' finalist",
        "personality": "Confident, strong, will show pride and a hint of anxiety when faced with questioning",
        "isMainCharacter": true
      },
      {
        "id": "character2",
        "name": "Andrei Ivanov",
        "identity": "'Dance Miracle' backstage staff, in charge of lighting",
        "personality": "Taciturn, observant, knows a little about dance, seems to be hiding some secrets",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      }
    ],
    "roundContents": [
      {
        "round": 1,
        "plot": "On the night of the final, Emilia is about to go on stage. The backstage atmosphere is tense, with all kinds of discussions. Andrei silently adjusts the lights, seemingly indifferent to everything around him. Emilia is doing her final preparations in the dressing room, she can feel the pressure from all sides. A reporter suddenly bursts into the dressing room, trying to interview Emilia about the rumors of plagiarism. Emilia angrily refuses the interview and claims that she will prove everything on stage. At the same time, Andrei finds an old photo in a corner backstage. The photo is of a young Victor and a young woman, with the woman's back to the camera, her face unclear. The back of the photo says: 'Victor and his Muse.'",
        "privateClues": {
          "character1": "Received an anonymous text message: 'Your dance moves are stolen! Victor is watching you.' This makes you more anxious and also makes you suspicious of the people around you.",
          "character2": "There are also some faint words on the back of the photo, which can only be seen at a specific angle of light. It seems to be: '...Amy...truth...protect...'"
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 2,
        "plot": "Emilia's performance is stunning, but there are some minor incidents during the process. At the climax, the lights suddenly fail for a short time. Although they are quickly restored, it has already affected Emilia's mood. After the performance, Emilia questions the backstage manager, but is told that the lighting equipment is all normal, and it may have been caused by a voltage fluctuation. Emilia suspects that someone is deliberately causing trouble. Andrei comes over at this time and tells Emilia in a low voice that he saw someone loitering near the lighting control room, but he didn't see who it was. He is willing to help investigate this matter. Emilia agrees to Andrei's help, but her heart is still full of doubts. Andrei begins to investigate secretly. He finds that the log records of the lighting control system have been tampered with, and the time is exactly during Emilia's performance.",
        "privateClues": {
          "character1": "You find that your dance shoes have been tampered with. The soles seem to have been smeared with some substance, which caused you to slip a little during the performance. You are more convinced that someone wants to frame you.",
          "character2": "You find a torn piece of paper in the trash can of the lighting control room, which says: '...must stop...Victor...public...'"
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 3,
        "plot": "Emilia decides to announce the truth at the awards ceremony. She finds Victor's dance partner from back then and learns from her that Victor did create a stunning set of dance moves, but for some reason they were not made public. Emilia realizes that the rumors are not groundless, but her dance moves are not plagiarism, but inspired by Victor's work. Andrei finds Emilia, gives her the torn paper and the old photo, and tells her that the lighting failure was not an accident, but man-made. He suspects that someone does not want Emilia to win the competition, so as to cover up Victor's secret back then. At the awards ceremony, Emilia bravely tells Victor's story and declares that her dance moves are a tribute to Victor, not plagiarism. In the end, Emilia wins the competition and also wins respect. Andrei also finds the real culprit in the lighting control room. It turns out to be the agent of another contestant. He was worried that Emilia would win the championship again, thus affecting the development of his artist, so he planned all this.",
        "privateClues": {
          "character1": "You notice that Andrei's eyes are always thoughtful, as if he is hiding many secrets. You decide to test him and ask him about Victor to see if he knows anything.",
          "character2": "In the control room, you find a list of the finalists. Emilia's name has been crossed out in red pen. Next to the list is a bottle of ointment for muscle soreness, the brand is very obscure."
        }
      }
    ],
    "createdAt": 1754467207980,
    "createdBy": "system"
  },
  {
    "id": "script_1754467511665_juaqucq6w",
    "title": "Watermelon Field Mystery",
    "rounds": 3,
    "background": "In the scorching summer, watermelon is a great way to relieve the heat. Green Water Village holds a lively watermelon-eating contest every year, and this year is no exception. However, this year's competition is shrouded in a strange atmosphere. The prize money for the competition, which was only for fun in previous years, is ridiculously high this year. It is rumored that it is sponsored by the mysterious wealthy merchant Li Yuanwai, who is new to the village. What is even more disturbing is that the watermelons used in the competition in previous years were all grown by Old Wang at the head of the village, but this year they have been replaced with 'Black Beauty' provided by Li Yuanwai. On the eve of the competition, the old cat in the village, 'Heizi,' suddenly died for no reason, and some people even claimed to have heard strange noises from the watermelon field in the middle of the night. The air is filled with the sweet smell of watermelon, and also a hint of an indescribable conspiracy. What is the secret behind this seemingly simple watermelon-eating contest? And who will be the final winner, or victim, of this game?",
    "characters": [
      {
        "id": "character1",
        "name": "Wang Dazhuang",
        "identity": "An honest melon farmer, and also the perennial champion of the village's watermelon-eating contest",
        "personality": "Honest and simple, strong, with an amazing speed of eating watermelons, a bit self-abased, but has an unyielding spirit in his bones.",
        "isMainCharacter": true
      },
      {
        "id": "character2",
        "name": "Li Yuanwai",
        "identity": "A wealthy merchant who has newly moved to the village, mysterious and generous",
        "personality": "A smiling tiger, sinister and cunning, with a deep mind, and an unusual enthusiasm for the watermelon competition.",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      },
      {
        "id": "character3",
        "name": "Zhang Cuihua",
        "identity": "The village's gossip queen, well-informed, loves to join in the fun",
        "personality": "Enthusiastic and cheerful, with a loud voice, likes to inquire about all kinds of gossip, but is not a bad person.",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      }
    ],
    "roundContents": [
      {
        "round": 1,
        "plot": "The competition officially begins, with gongs and drums and firecrackers. The crowd of villagers is huge, and the cheers are deafening. Wang Dazhuang stands in the most conspicuous position. He looks at the mountain of Black Beauty watermelons in front of him, takes a deep breath, and tries to calm his inner tension. Li Yuanwai, dressed in a silk robe, stands aside with a smile, but his eyes are unfathomable. Zhang Cuihua squeezes to the front of the crowd, shouting and cheering at the top of her lungs, and from time to time muttering something to the people around her. The rules of the competition are simple: whoever eats the most watermelons in the allotted time wins. At the referee's command, the contestants pick up the watermelons and start eating ravenously. Wang Dazhuang is indeed an old hand at eating watermelons. He chooses a large and round watermelon and eats more than half of it in a few bites. Li Yuanwai always has a smile on his face, applauding from time to time, but his eyes are always on Wang Dazhuang, as if observing something. Zhang Cuihua looks around, sometimes at Wang Dazhuang, sometimes at Li Yuanwai, and keeps muttering: 'This year's melons seem a bit different, not as sweet as in previous years.' Halfway through the competition, Wang Dazhuang suddenly feels dizzy, but he grits his teeth, endures the discomfort, and continues to eat. Seeing Wang Dazhuang's pale face, Li Yuanwai's mouth shows a faint, imperceptible smile. Zhang Cuihua begins to suspect that there is something wrong with the melons and inquires everywhere to find out their origin.",
        "privateClues": {
          "character1": "The watermelon provided by Li Yuanwai tastes a bit strange, not like ordinary Black Beauty, and I feel a little dizzy after eating it. (58 characters)",
          "character2": "Wang Dazhuang's eating speed is very fast, but his face is getting worse and worse. It seems the plan is going smoothly. The stuff added to the Black Beauty will take effect soon. (65 characters)",
          "character3": "This watermelon tastes wrong today. If you smell it carefully, there seems to be a faint almond smell! I heard that Li Yuanwai recently opened a medicinal herb shop in the village. (72 characters)"
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 2,
        "plot": "Wang Dazhuang's head is getting dizzier and dizzier, and he starts to see double. He realizes that he may have fallen into a trap. He forces himself to slow down his eating speed, trying to relieve his discomfort. Li Yuanwai seems to have noticed Wang Dazhuang's abnormality. He walks up to Wang Dazhuang and asks hypocritically: 'Brother Wang, are you okay? Do you want to take a break?' Wang Dazhuang shakes his head. He knows that if he stops, he will lose completely. Zhang Cuihua finally finds out the origin of the watermelons. She learns that these watermelons were indeed provided by Li Yuanwai, and were bought from a merchant from another place. It is said that this kind of Black Beauty is a new variety and is particularly sweet. But Zhang Cuihua always feels that things are not that simple. She remembers the death of the old cat Heizi in the village, and the faint almond smell in the watermelon, and her heart is full of doubts. She decides to find a chance to talk to Wang Dazhuang. Just then, Wang Dazhuang suddenly feels a sharp pain. He clutches his stomach, his face as pale as paper. He can't hold on any longer and collapses to the ground. The crowd of villagers is in an uproar. Li Yuanwai immediately steps forward to check, pretending to be concerned: 'Brother Wang, what's wrong with you? Quick, call a doctor!' Seeing this, Zhang Cuihua immediately squeezes to Wang Dazhuang's side and says in a low voice: 'Dazhuang, there's something wrong with this melon! Be careful of Li Yuanwai!' Wang Dazhuang raises his head with difficulty, looks at Zhang Cuihua, and his eyes are full of gratitude.",
        "privateClues": {
          "character1": "Zhang Cuihua told me that there is something wrong with the watermelon and asked me to be careful of Li Yuanwai. Is this all Li Yuanwai's doing? Why would he do this? (62 characters)",
          "character2": "Wang Dazhuang has finally fallen. It seems the dose was just right. That old gossip Zhang Cuihua, how dare she ruin my good plan! It seems I need to find a chance to shut her up. (68 characters)",
          "character3": "It seems my guess was right, there is indeed something wrong with this watermelon! Li Yuanwai must be up to something! I have to find a way to expose his true colors and not let honest people suffer! (75 characters)"
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 3,
        "plot": "Wang Dazhuang is sent to the village clinic, and the doctor diagnoses him with food poisoning. Li Yuanwai insists that it is a quality problem with the watermelon and says he will bear all the medical expenses. But Wang Dazhuang and Zhang Cuihua both know that this is by no means ordinary food poisoning. Zhang Cuihua decides to risk investigating Li Yuanwai. She secretly sneaks into Li Yuanwai's residence and searches for evidence everywhere. She finds a suspicious bottle with the words 'amygdalin' on it. She immediately realizes that this is the culprit that caused Wang Dazhuang's poisoning. At the same time, Wang Dazhuang also struggles to get out of bed. He knows he can't just sit back and wait. He decides to confront Li Yuanwai. He comes to Li Yuanwai's residence and happens to run into Zhang Cuihua who is searching for evidence. The two exchange a look and immediately understand each other's intentions. Li Yuanwai suddenly appears, holding a dagger in his hand, with a ferocious expression on his face: 'Since you both know, then you can both go to hell!' Wang Dazhuang and Zhang Cuihua fight back with all their might, and a fierce battle begins. In the end, Wang Dazhuang, with his superior strength, subdues Li Yuanwai. It turns out that Li Yuanwai is not an ordinary wealthy merchant, but a drug smuggler. He sponsored the watermelon-eating contest to cover up his activities, mixing drugs into the watermelons and then transporting them to other places through the competition. And Wang Dazhuang, as the perennial champion of the watermelon-eating contest, naturally became the biggest obstacle in his plan. The truth is revealed, and the villagers are furious, taking Li Yuanwai to the police station. Although Wang Dazhuang is weak, his heart is full of justice and courage. He knows that he has done the right thing.",
        "privateClues": {
          "character1": "Amygdalin! So that's it, Li Yuanwai wanted to use the watermelon-eating contest to smuggle drugs! Fortunately, Cuihua and I discovered his conspiracy and stopped him! (63 characters)",
          "character2": "The plan failed! Those two idiots, Wang Dazhuang and Zhang Cuihua, ruined my big plan! But it doesn't matter, I still have a chance to make a comeback! (58 characters)",
          "character3": "The truth is finally out! Li Yuanwai is really a criminal! Fortunately, Dazhuang and I stopped him, otherwise who knows how many people would have been harmed! (60 characters)"
        }
      }
    ],
    "createdAt": 1754467511665,
    "createdBy": "system"
  },
  {
    "id": "script_1754467916276_3ed4ge1h0",
    "title": "The Curse of Moonshadow Village",
    "rounds": 3,
    "background": "Legend has it that in the far east, there is a village blessed by the moonlight but shrouded in a curse - Moonshadow Village. Every full moon night, the village is enveloped in a strange purple mist, and the villagers go mad and kill each other. This terrifying scene has been going on for hundreds of years, but no one has been able to break it. Until one day, a young man who called himself an onmyoji, Usagi, came to Moonshadow Village with his loyal shikigami, Hachi. Usagi had heard the legend of Moonshadow Village and was determined to use his own power to uncover the truth of the curse and save the villagers shrouded in darkness. He knew that this was not only to help others, but also to prove his own ability and wash away the shame of his family. His family was once a powerful onmyoji family, but they failed in an exorcism ceremony and have since declined. Whether Usagi can succeed is still unknown. But in his eyes, a raging fire is burning, which is the desire for the truth and the hope for the future. He firmly believes that as long as he finds the source of the curse, he will be able to break the shadow that hangs over Moonshadow Village. And Hachi will always be by his side, becoming his most solid backing.",
    "characters": [
      {
        "id": "usagi",
        "name": "Usagi",
        "identity": "Young onmyoji",
        "personality": "Calm, persistent, a bit conceited, eager to prove himself",
        "isMainCharacter": true
      },
      {
        "id": "oldManKenji",
        "name": "Grandpa Kenji",
        "identity": "The village chief of Moonshadow Village, old and wise",
        "personality": "Worried, weathered, has a deep understanding of the village's curse",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      },
      {
        "id": "midori",
        "name": "Midori",
        "identity": "The young miko of Moonshadow Village",
        "personality": "Mysterious, taciturn, has the ability to perceive the curse",
        "isMainCharacter": false
      }
    ],
    "roundContents": [
      {
        "round": 1,
        "plot": "Usagi and Hachi arrive at Moonshadow Village. The village is shrouded in a depressing atmosphere, the houses are dilapidated, and the villagers' faces are filled with fear and numbness. The air is filled with a faint smell of blood and decay, which makes people feel uncomfortable. Usagi first visits the village chief, Grandpa Kenji, hoping to learn more about the curse. Grandpa Kenji tremblingly leads Usagi into a dim room filled with old sacrificial items. He tells Usagi that the earliest record of the curse can be traced back hundreds of years, when the village worshiped a powerful moon god, but because of the villagers' blasphemy, the moon god sent down a punishment. Since then, a tragedy has occurred every full moon night. Grandpa Kenji also mentioned that there is a young miko in the village, Midori, who may be able to perceive the root of the curse. Usagi bids farewell to Grandpa Kenji and decides to visit Midori. Midori lives in a simple hut on the edge of the village. The hut is dim and damp, with a smell of herbs. When Midori sees Usagi, she does not show any surprise, but just looks at him silently. Usagi explains his purpose and hopes she can help. Midori is silent for a moment, then slowly says: 'The power of the curse is strengthening, the full moon night is coming, and we don't have much time left. Go to the ancient shrine in the center of the village, the answer may be hidden there.' After saying that, Midori closes her eyes and says no more.",
        "privateClues": {
          "usagi": "Grandpa Kenji mentioned that the village once blasphemed the moon god, which led to the curse. Does this mean that the curse is not unbreakable, but can be lifted by obtaining the moon god's forgiveness in some way?",
          "oldManKenji": "The ancient shrine in the center of the village is the oldest building in the village and the place where successive village chiefs held sacrificial ceremonies. There seems to be some secret hidden in the shrine, but no one dares to approach it.",
          "midori": "My perception tells me that the core of the curse is not the moon god, but some evil thing sealed under the shrine. The moon god is just taking the blame."
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 2,
        "plot": "Following Midori's guidance, Usagi and Hachi come to the ancient shrine in the center of the village. The shrine is dilapidated, covered with dust and cobwebs. The main gate of the shrine is tightly closed, and it is engraved with ancient runes that emit a faint light. Usagi carefully observes these runes and finds that they seem to be an ancient sealing technique. He tries to break the seal, but finds that these runes contain powerful energy, and it is difficult for him to break them easily with his current strength. Just as Usagi is feeling helpless, Grandpa Kenji slowly walks over with a cane. He tells Usagi that these runes were carved by the first village chief to seal the evil thing under the shrine. Grandpa Kenji also says that only a miko with a pure bloodline can open the gate of the shrine. At this time, Midori also comes to the shrine. She walks to the gate and slowly chants an ancient spell. As the spell is chanted, the runes on the gate begin to flicker, emitting a dazzling light. Suddenly, with a loud noise, the gate of the shrine slowly opens. Behind the gate is a dark passage leading to the underground. A cold breath rushes out, making people feel creepy. Grandpa Kenji's face is pale, and he trembles as he says: 'This is the source of the curse, you must be careful!' Usagi takes a deep breath, tightens his grip on his magical weapon, and leads Hachi and Midori into the dark passage.",
        "privateClues": {
          "usagi": "Grandpa Kenji mentioned that only a miko with a pure bloodline can open the shrine gate. Midori's process of opening the gate was very smooth, and she was very familiar with the spell. Does this mean that she is a descendant of the first miko and has some knowledge of the situation under the shrine?",
          "oldManKenji": "The first village chief once warned his descendants that they must never open the gate of the shrine, otherwise it would release an uncontrollable evil force. But now, in order to save the village, there is no other choice.",
          "midori": "The power of the first miko flows in my blood. I must guide them on the right path, even if it means I will pay a price. There is a trap in the passage, be careful."
        }
      },
      {
        "round": 3,
        "plot": "Usagi and his party slowly advance along the dark passage. The passage is deep and long, and the walls are covered with distorted murals depicting various terrifying scenes. The air is filled with a strong smell of sulfur, which makes people feel suffocated. Suddenly, Midori stops, her face turning pale. She points ahead and says: 'There is a trap ahead, be careful!' Usagi uses his onmyojutsu and finds that the ground ahead is covered with hidden magic circles. Once these magic circles are touched, they will trigger a powerful attack. Usagi carefully avoids the magic circles and leads everyone to continue forward. Finally, they reach the end of the passage. At the end of the passage is a wide underground altar. In the center of the altar stands a huge stone statue. The stone statue has a ferocious face and exudes an evil aura. Below the stone statue, a black vortex is slowly rotating, which is the source of the curse. Suddenly, the stone statue lets out a low roar, and the ground begins to shake. From the body of the stone statue, a figure slowly walks out. It is a mysterious person in a black robe. He smiles grimly and says: 'You're finally here, I've been waiting for a long time.' The mysterious person admits that he is the real creator of the curse. He used the power of the moon god to turn the village into his experimental field. He needs more souls to maintain his power. A fierce battle is about to break out. Usagi knows that in order to save Moonshadow Village, he must defeat this mysterious person. He and Hachi launch a fierce attack on the mysterious person, while Midori silently chants a spell on the side to support them. After a fierce battle, Usagi finally finds the mysterious person's weakness and successfully defeats him. As the mysterious person falls, the black vortex also disappears, and the curse that has been hanging over Moonshadow Village is finally lifted.",
        "privateClues": {
          "usagi": "The mysterious person used the power of the moon god, which means that the moon god itself is not malicious, but was just used. Perhaps there is a way to appease the moon god's anger and completely eliminate the hidden danger of the curse.",
          "oldManKenji": "Although the curse has been lifted, the villagers' hearts have been greatly traumatized. It will take time to heal their wounds and rebuild the village.",
          "midori": "Although the mysterious person has been defeated, the evil aura he left behind still exists. A purification ceremony is needed to completely eliminate the hidden danger. I will stay in the village and guard this place."
        }
      }
    ],
    "createdAt": 1754467916276,
    "createdBy": "system"
  },
